{
 "0001": {
  "title": "",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_01\" id=\"tag_17_434_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "pthread_join — wait for thread termination",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_02\" id=\"tag_17_434_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/pthread.h.html\">pthread.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint pthread_join(pthread_t</tt> <i>thread</i><tt>, void **</tt><i>value_ptr</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_03\" id=\"tag_17_434_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]pthread_join[/I5]() function shall suspend execution of the calling thread until the target [I6]thread[/I6] terminates,\nunless the target [I7]thread[/I7] has already terminated. On return from a successful [I8]pthread_join[/I8]() call with a non-NULL\n[I9]value_ptr[/I9] argument, the value passed to [A10][I11]pthread_exit[/I11]()[/A10] by the\nterminating thread shall be made available in the location referenced by [I12]value_ptr[/I12]. When a [I13]pthread_join[/I13]() returns\nsuccessfully, the target thread has been terminated. The results of multiple simultaneous calls to [I14]pthread_join[/I14]() specifying\nthe same target thread are undefined. If the thread calling [I15]pthread_join[/I15]() is canceled, then the target thread shall not be\ndetached.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A10": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pthread_exit.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "It is unspecified whether a zombie thread counts against {PTHREAD_THREADS_MAX}.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The behavior is undefined if the value specified by the [I16]thread[/I16] argument to [I17]pthread_join[/I17]() does not refer to a\njoinable thread.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The behavior is undefined if the value specified by the [I18]thread[/I18] argument to [I19]pthread_join[/I19]() refers to the calling\nthread.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If [I20]thread[/I20] refers to a thread that was created using [A21][I22]thrd_create[/I22]()[/A21] and\nthe thread terminates, or has already terminated, by returning from its start routine, the behavior of [I23]pthread_join[/I23]() is\nundefined. If [I24]thread[/I24] refers to a thread that terminates, or has already terminated, by calling [A25][I26]thrd_exit[/I26]()[/A25], the behavior of [I27]pthread_join[/I27]() is undefined.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A21": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/thrd_create.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I22": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A25": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/thrd_exit.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00011",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A28][/A28]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_04\" id=\"tag_17_434_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "If successful, the [I29]pthread_join[/I29]() function shall return zero; otherwise, an error number shall be returned to indicate\nthe error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00013",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A30][/A30]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_05\" id=\"tag_17_434_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I31]pthread_join[/I31]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00015",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EDEADLK]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00016",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "A deadlock was detected.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00017",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I32]pthread_join[/I32]() function shall not return an error code of [EINTR].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00018",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A33][/A33]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A33": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_06\" id=\"tag_17_434_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "An example of thread creation and deletion follows:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A34][/A34]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_07\" id=\"tag_17_434_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00022",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A35][/A35]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A35": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_434_08\" id=\"tag_17_434_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00023",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I36]pthread_join[/I36]() function is a convenience that has proven useful in multi-threaded applications. It is true that a\nprogrammer could simulate this function if it were not provided by passing extra state as part of the argument to the\n[I37]start_routine[/I37](). The terminating thread would set a flag to indicate termination and broadcast a condition that is part of\nthat state; a joining thread would wait on that condition variable. While such a technique would allow a thread to wait on more\ncomplex conditions (for example, waiting for multiple threads to terminate), waiting on individual thread termination is considered\nwidely useful. Also, including the [I38]pthread_join[/I38]() function in no way precludes a programmer from coding such complex waits.\nThus, while not a primitive, including [I39]pthread_join[/I39]() in this volume of POSIX.1-2024 was considered valuable.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00024",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I40]pthread_join[/I40]() function provides a simple mechanism allowing an application to wait for a thread to terminate. After\nthe thread terminates, the application may then choose to clean up resources that were used by the thread. For instance, after\n[I41]pthread_join[/I41]() returns, any application-provided stack storage could be reclaimed.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00025",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I42]pthread_join[/I42]() or [A43][I44]pthread_detach[/I44]()[/A43] function should eventually\nbe called for every thread that is created with the [I45]detachstate[/I45] attribute set to PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE so that storage\nassociated with the thread may be reclaimed.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I42": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A43": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pthread_detach.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I45": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00026",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The interaction between [I46]pthread_join[/I46]() and cancellation is well-defined for the following reasons:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00027",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     9,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I47]pthread_join[/I47]() function, like all other non-async-cancel-safe functions, can only be called with deferred\ncancelability type.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00028",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     9,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Cancellation cannot occur in the disabled cancelability state.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00029",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     11
    ],
    "text": "Thus, only the default cancelability state need be considered. As specified, either the [I48]pthread_join[/I48]() call is canceled,\nor it succeeds, but not both. The difference is obvious to the application, since either a cancellation handler is run or\n[I49]pthread_join[/I49]() returns. There are no race conditions since [I50]pthread_join[/I50]() was called in the deferred cancelability\nstate.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I48": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00030",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     13
    ],
    "text": "If an implementation detects that the value specified by the [I51]thread[/I51] argument to [I52]pthread_join[/I52]() does not refer to a\njoinable thread, it is recommended that the function should fail and report an [EINVAL] error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00031",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     15
    ],
    "text": "If an implementation detects that the value specified by the [I53]thread[/I53] argument to [I54]pthread_join[/I54]() refers to the\ncalling thread, it is recommended that the function should fail and report an [EDEADLK] error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00032",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     17
    ],
    "text": "If an implementation detects use of a thread ID after the end of its lifetime, it is recommended that the function should fail\nand report an [ESRCH] error.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00033",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     19
    ],
    "text": "The [I55]pthread_join[/I55]() function cannot be used to obtain the exit status of a thread that was created using [A56][I57]thrd_create[/I57]()[/A56] and which terminates by returning from its start routine, or of a thread\nthat terminates by calling [A58][I59]thrd_exit[/I59]()[/A58], because such threads have an [B60]int[/B60]\nexit status, instead of the [B61]void&nbsp;*[/B61] that [I62]pthread_join[/I62]() returns via its [I63]value_ptr[/I63] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A56": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/thrd_create.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I57": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/thrd_exit.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I59": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B60": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B61": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I62": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I63": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00034",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     47
    ],
    "text": "[A64][/A64]FUTURE DIRECTIONS",
    "placeholders": {
